finding: 1. src/cli/publish.ts:365 (also src/cli/index.ts:73-74 and README.md:107-109): CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID does not bind rollback/delete to the linked account. Pinned Wrangler 4.151.3 getActiveAccountId gives discovered config.account_id precedence over that environment variable (node_modules/wrangler/wrangler-dist/cli.js:133611-133625); both handlers use requireAuth(config). An existing project/ancestor Wrangler config naming account B makes the printed command for account A roll back or delete the same-named Worker in B. The parse checks run in a clean scaffold and delete --dry-run bypasses requireAuth, so both tests pass despite this failure. 2. src/cli/publish.ts:365,435: the report prints actionable unpublish instructions without the person-confirmation requirement, including a Wrangler delete that auto-confirms noninteractively. An agent following the report alone can delete without seeking confirmation; help, README and skill carry the warning, but the report does not route to them. src/cli/publish-report.test.ts:95-118 asserts command strings but not this safety guidance, so passes with the omission.
